{
  "title": "Stage 4: Credits and GPA",
  "summary": "Read a second input section, Join scores to course credits for a weighted GPA, and GroupJoin to find courses nobody took.",
  "minutes": 18,
  "steps": [
    {
      "type": "learn",
      "title": "Briefing: a second section and a join",
      "body": [
        "A GPA weights each course by its **credits**, and credits live in a second section of the input after a `[courses]` marker:",
        "",
        "```text",
        "student,course,score",
        "Ada,Math,91",
        "Ada,Physics,78",
        "Ada,History,84",
        "Ben,Math,85",
        "Ben,Physics,64",
        "Cy,Math,88",
        "Cy,Physics,92",
        "Cy,History,100",
        "Dee,Math,88",
        "Dee,Physics,55",
        "Dee,History,97",
        "Eve,Math,59",
        "Eve,History,84",
        "",
        "[courses]",
        "Math,4",
        "Physics,3",
        "History,2",
        "```",
        "",
        "Splitting the input in two is LINQ as well. `TakeWhile` reads up to the marker; `SkipWhile` jumps to it and `Skip(1)` steps past it:",
        "",
        "```csharp fragment",
        "var scoreLines  = lines.TakeWhile(l => l.Trim() != \"[courses]\").ToList();",
        "var courseLines = lines.SkipWhile(l => l.Trim() != \"[courses]\").Skip(1);",
        "```",
        "",
        "With no marker, `scoreLines` is everything and `courseLines` is empty, so old input keeps working.",
        "",
        "Then `Join` pairs each score with the course whose name matches, like a SQL inner join:",
        "",
        "```csharp fragment",
        "scores.Join(courses,",
        "    s => s.Course,          // key on the left",
        "    c => c.Name,            // key on the right",
        "    (s, c) => new { s.Student, c.Credits, Points = GradePoints(Letter(s.Points)) })",
        "```",
        "",
        "A score whose course has no credits row simply has no partner, so the join leaves it out. The weighted GPA is `Sum(points × credits) / Sum(credits)`. Grade points are A = 4, B = 3, C = 2, D = 1, F = 0, using the letter of each single score."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "predict",
      "prompt": "Splitting at a marker. What does this print?",
      "code": [
        "var lines = new[] { \"a\", \"b\", \"[x]\", \"c\", \"d\" };",
        "",
        "var before = lines.TakeWhile(l => l != \"[x]\");",
        "var after = lines.SkipWhile(l => l != \"[x]\").Skip(1);",
        "",
        "Console.WriteLine(string.Join(\",\", before));",
        "Console.WriteLine(string.Join(\",\", after));"
      ],
      "answer": [
        "a,b",
        "c,d"
      ],
      "explain": "`TakeWhile` stops at the marker without including it. `SkipWhile` stops skipping *at* the marker, so it is still the first item, and `Skip(1)` drops it."
    },
    {
      "type": "predict",
      "prompt": "`Join` only keeps matches. What does this print?",
      "code": [
        "var scores = new[] { (\"Ada\", \"Math\"), (\"Ada\", \"Music\"), (\"Ben\", \"Math\") };",
        "var credits = new[] { (\"Math\", 4), (\"Art\", 2) };",
        "",
        "var joined = scores.Join(credits,",
        "    s => s.Item2,",
        "    c => c.Item1,",
        "    (s, c) => $\"{s.Item1}:{c.Item2}\");",
        "",
        "Console.WriteLine(string.Join(\" \", joined));"
      ],
      "answer": "Ada:4 Ben:4",
      "explain": "Only the two Math scores have a partner. Music has no credits row and Art has no scores, so an inner join drops both."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "title": "Weighted GPA",
      "carry": true,
      "prompt": [
        "Read the optional `[courses]` section and print a weighted GPA.",
        "",
        "1. Split `lines` at a line that is `[courses]`: scores come before it, `name,credits` lines after it. Parse courses into `record Course(string Name, int Credits);` with a `TryParseCourse` that skips bad lines (2 columns, credits a positive whole number).",
        "2. Only when there is at least one course, print an empty line, `GPA:`, then one line per student: `Name: gpa (N credits)`, GPA to two decimal places, best GPA first, ties by name.",
        "3. Use `Join` to pair scores with courses. Scores for a course with no credits row do not count toward GPA.",
        "4. Write `int GradePoints(string letter)` as a switch expression.",
        "",
        "Everything from earlier stages must still print first. For this input:",
        "",
        "```text",
        "student,course,score",
        "Ada,Math,91",
        "Ada,Physics,78",
        "Ada,History,84",
        "Ben,Math,85",
        "Ben,Physics,64",
        "Cy,Math,88",
        "Cy,Physics,92",
        "Cy,History,100",
        "Dee,Math,88",
        "Dee,Physics,55",
        "Dee,History,97",
        "Eve,Math,59",
        "Eve,History,84",
        "",
        "[courses]",
        "Math,4",
        "Physics,3",
        "History,2",
        "```",
        "",
        "print exactly:",
        "",
        "```text",
        "Scores: 13, skipped: 0",
        "",
        "Averages:",
        "Ada: 84.3 B",
        "Ben: 74.5 C",
        "Cy: 93.3 A",
        "Dee: 80.0 B",
        "Eve: 71.5 C",
        "",
        "Rankings:",
        "History",
        "  1. Cy 100",
        "  2. Dee 97",
        "  3. Ada 84",
        "  3. Eve 84",
        "  lowest: Ada 84",
        "Math",
        "  1. Ada 91",
        "  2. Cy 88",
        "  2. Dee 88",
        "  lowest: Eve 59",
        "Physics",
        "  1. Cy 92",
        "  2. Ada 78",
        "  3. Ben 64",
        "  lowest: Dee 55",
        "",
        "GPA:",
        "Cy: 3.56 (9 credits)",
        "Ada: 3.11 (9 credits)",
        "Dee: 2.22 (9 credits)",
        "Ben: 2.14 (7 credits)",
        "Eve: 1.00 (6 credits)",
        "```"
      ],
      "starter": [
        "var lines = new List<string>();",
        "string? line;",
        "while ((line = Console.ReadLine()) is not null)",
        "    lines.Add(line);",
        "",
        "var rows = lines",
        "    .Where(l => !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(l))",
        "    .Where(l => !l.StartsWith(\"student,\"))",
        "    .ToList();",
        "",
        "var scores = rows",
        "    .Select(TryParseScore)",
        "    .OfType<Score>()",
        "    .ToList();",
        "",
        "Console.WriteLine($\"Scores: {scores.Count}, skipped: {rows.Count - scores.Count}\");",
        "",
        "var averages = scores",
        "    .GroupBy(s => s.Student)",
        "    .Select(g => new { Student = g.Key, Average = g.Average(s => s.Points) })",
        "    .OrderBy(a => a.Student)",
        "    .ToList();",
        "",
        "Console.WriteLine();",
        "Console.WriteLine(\"Averages:\");",
        "foreach (var a in averages)",
        "    Console.WriteLine($\"{a.Student}: {a.Average:F1} {Letter(a.Average)}\");",
        "",
        "Console.WriteLine();",
        "Console.WriteLine(\"Rankings:\");",
        "foreach (var course in scores.GroupBy(s => s.Course).OrderBy(g => g.Key))",
        "{",
        "    var ranked = course",
        "        .OrderByDescending(s => s.Points)",
        "        .ThenBy(s => s.Student)",
        "        .ToList();",
        "",
        "    var cutoff = ranked.Take(3).Last().Points;",
        "",
        "    Console.WriteLine(course.Key);",
        "    foreach (var s in ranked.TakeWhile(s => s.Points >= cutoff))",
        "    {",
        "        var rank = 1 + ranked.Count(other => other.Points > s.Points);",
        "        Console.WriteLine($\"  {rank}. {s.Student} {s.Points}\");",
        "    }",
        "",
        "    var lowest = ranked.MinBy(s => s.Points)!;",
        "    Console.WriteLine($\"  lowest: {lowest.Student} {lowest.Points}\");",
        "}",
        "",
        "Score? TryParseScore(string line)",
        "{",
        "    var parts = line.Split(',');",
        "    if (parts.Length != 3) return null;",
        "    if (!int.TryParse(parts[2], out var points)) return null;",
        "    if (points < 0 || points > 100) return null;",
        "    return new Score(parts[0].Trim(), parts[1].Trim(), points);",
        "}",
        "",
        "string Letter(double average) => average switch",
        "{",
        "    >= 90 => \"A\",",
        "    >= 80 => \"B\",",
        "    >= 70 => \"C\",",
        "    >= 60 => \"D\",",
        "    _ => \"F\"",
        "};",
        "",
        "record Score(string Student, string Course, int Points);"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "var lines = new List<string>();",
        "string? line;",
        "while ((line = Console.ReadLine()) is not null)",
        "    lines.Add(line);",
        "",
        "var scoreLines = lines",
        "    .TakeWhile(l => l.Trim() != \"[courses]\")",
        "    .ToList();",
        "",
        "var courses = lines",
        "    .SkipWhile(l => l.Trim() != \"[courses]\")",
        "    .Skip(1)",
        "    .Where(l => !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(l))",
        "    .Select(TryParseCourse)",
        "    .OfType<Course>()",
        "    .ToList();",
        "",
        "var rows = scoreLines",
        "    .Where(l => !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(l))",
        "    .Where(l => !l.StartsWith(\"student,\"))",
        "    .ToList();",
        "",
        "var scores = rows",
        "    .Select(TryParseScore)",
        "    .OfType<Score>()",
        "    .ToList();",
        "",
        "Console.WriteLine($\"Scores: {scores.Count}, skipped: {rows.Count - scores.Count}\");",
        "",
        "var averages = scores",
        "    .GroupBy(s => s.Student)",
        "    .Select(g => new { Student = g.Key, Average = g.Average(s => s.Points) })",
        "    .OrderBy(a => a.Student)",
        "    .ToList();",
        "",
        "Console.WriteLine();",
        "Console.WriteLine(\"Averages:\");",
        "foreach (var a in averages)",
        "    Console.WriteLine($\"{a.Student}: {a.Average:F1} {Letter(a.Average)}\");",
        "",
        "Console.WriteLine();",
        "Console.WriteLine(\"Rankings:\");",
        "foreach (var course in scores.GroupBy(s => s.Course).OrderBy(g => g.Key))",
        "{",
        "    var ranked = course",
        "        .OrderByDescending(s => s.Points)",
        "        .ThenBy(s => s.Student)",
        "        .ToList();",
        "",
        "    var cutoff = ranked.Take(3).Last().Points;",
        "",
        "    Console.WriteLine(course.Key);",
        "    foreach (var s in ranked.TakeWhile(s => s.Points >= cutoff))",
        "    {",
        "        var rank = 1 + ranked.Count(other => other.Points > s.Points);",
        "        Console.WriteLine($\"  {rank}. {s.Student} {s.Points}\");",
        "    }",
        "",
        "    var lowest = ranked.MinBy(s => s.Points)!;",
        "    Console.WriteLine($\"  lowest: {lowest.Student} {lowest.Points}\");",
        "}",
        "",
        "if (courses.Count > 0)",
        "{",
        "    var gpas = scores",
        "        .Join(courses,",
        "            s => s.Course,",
        "            c => c.Name,",
        "            (s, c) => new { s.Student, c.Credits, Points = GradePoints(Letter(s.Points)) })",
        "        .GroupBy(x => x.Student)",
        "        .Select(g => new",
        "        {",
        "            Student = g.Key,",
        "            Credits = g.Sum(x => x.Credits),",
        "            Gpa = (double)g.Sum(x => x.Points * x.Credits) / g.Sum(x => x.Credits)",
        "        })",
        "        .OrderByDescending(x => x.Gpa)",
        "        .ThenBy(x => x.Student)",
        "        .ToList();",
        "",
        "    Console.WriteLine();",
        "    Console.WriteLine(\"GPA:\");",
        "    foreach (var g in gpas)",
        "        Console.WriteLine($\"{g.Student}: {g.Gpa:F2} ({g.Credits} credits)\");",
        "}",
        "",
        "Score? TryParseScore(string line)",
        "{",
        "    var parts = line.Split(',');",
        "    if (parts.Length != 3) return null;",
        "    if (!int.TryParse(parts[2], out var points)) return null;",
        "    if (points < 0 || points > 100) return null;",
        "    return new Score(parts[0].Trim(), parts[1].Trim(), points);",
        "}",
        "",
        "Course? TryParseCourse(string line)",
        "{",
        "    var parts = line.Split(',');",
        "    if (parts.Length != 2) return null;",
        "    if (!int.TryParse(parts[1], out var credits) || credits <= 0) return null;",
        "    return new Course(parts[0].Trim(), credits);",
        "}",
        "",
        "string Letter(double average) => average switch",
        "{",
        "    >= 90 => \"A\",",
        "    >= 80 => \"B\",",
        "    >= 70 => \"C\",",
        "    >= 60 => \"D\",",
        "    _ => \"F\"",
        "};",
        "",
        "int GradePoints(string letter) => letter switch",
        "{",
        "    \"A\" => 4,",
        "    \"B\" => 3,",
        "    \"C\" => 2,",
        "    \"D\" => 1,",
        "    _ => 0",
        "};",
        "",
        "record Score(string Student, string Course, int Points);",
        "",
        "record Course(string Name, int Credits);"
      ],
